{
  "//": "PULSE PUSH - tap to emit a shockwave that pushes the ball. Reach the goal ring, avoid the hazards. Clearing a level increments it and the field is rebuilt.",
  "//levels": "The field is a function of `level`. `curLvl` records what is currently built; when it differs from `level` the `rebuild` flag goes high and every entity equation takes its setup branch instead of its motion branch. curLvl catches up on its own, so the flag self-clears. Death sets curLvl to -1, which rebuilds the same level - one mechanism, two uses.",
  "//difficulty": "Three axes, not one multiplier: hazards activate progressively (one at level 1, two at level 2, three from level 3), the goal shrinks from r26 to a floor of r16, and everything moves faster with spd. Entity count is fixed at parse time, so 'more hazards' is done by gating collision and drawing rather than by creating particles.",
  "//setup": "Setup values are expressions in `level`, never constants: the goal walks a circle and the ball starts diametrically opposite it, so the two can never be generated on top of each other.",
  "//engine": "Expressions cap at 32 RPN tokens. ifElse(falseValue, trueValue, condition) reads its condition LAST. A particlesLoop evaluates in one pass - no equation sees a sibling's new value. See GUIDE.md.",
  "header": {
    "apiLevel": 7,
    "width": 400,
    "height": 400,
    "profiles": 513,
    "contentDescription": "Pulse Push: tap to push the ball to the goal without hitting a hazard"
  },
